#: g101/3d/101_3d_01.md
msgid "In this tutorial you learned how to use Godot's 3D editor, how to add 3D\nnodes such as {{< gd-icon Node3D >}}`Node3D`, {{< gd-icon MeshInstance3D >}}`MeshInstance3D`, and {{< gd-icon Camera3D >}}`Camera3D`, and how to use gizmos to place your objects. You also learned a bunch of new terminology. Hopefully you're not overwhelmed."
msgstr ""

#: g101/3d/101_3d_01.md
msgid "## Getting Started in 3D"
msgstr ""

#: g101/3d/101_3d_01.md
msgid "One of Godot's strengths is its ability to handle both 2D and 3D games. While\nmuch of what you've learned working on 2D projects (nodes, scenes, signals, etc.)\napplies equally well in 3D, there is also a whole new layer of complexity and\ncapabilities. First, you'll find that there are some additional features\navailable in the 3D editor window, so we'll start there:"
msgstr ""

#: g101/3d/101_3d_01.md
msgid "When you first open a new project in Godot, you will see the 3D project view:"
msgstr ""

#: g101/3d/101_3d_01.md
msgid "In addition, if you're familiar with popular 3D games, you might prefer _Freelook_\nmode, which you can toggle on/off using _Shift+F_. In this mode, you can use the\nWASD keys to fly around the scene while aiming with the mouse."
msgstr ""

#: g101/3d/101_3d_01.md
msgid "Take a few minutes to experiment and get familiar with the gizmo. Use Undo if\nyou find yourself getting lost."
msgstr ""

#: g101/3d/101_3d_01.md
msgid "By default, the gizmo controls operate in _global space_. When you rotate the\nobject, the gizmo's arrows still point along the axes. However, if you click\nthe **Use Local Space** button, the gizmo will switch to moving the body in\n_local space_."
msgstr ""

#: g101/3d/101_3d_01.md
msgid "You can also alter the camera's view by clicking on the `[Perspective]` label\nin the upper-left corner. Here, you can snap the camera to a particular\norientation."
msgstr ""

#: g101/3d/101_3d_01.md
msgid "In the next part, we'll look at how to build a 3D scene by importing 3D assets\nand how to use more of Godot's 3D nodes."
